<title>FRANCE: U.S. top destination for Paris Jan-Oct 96 exports.</title>
<headline>U.S. top destination for Paris Jan-Oct 96 exports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States was the principal destination for export traffic from the Paris airports between January and October 1996, Paris airport authority, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>The principal destinations by country for ADP exports during the period January-October 1996, with percentage change on January-October 1995, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  United States	    105,515 tonnes  down  0.2 pct</p>
<p> 2  Japan			 27,317 tonnes  down  6.9</p>
<p> 3  Hong Kong		   20,045 tonnes  up    0.2</p>
<p> 4  Canada			17,389 tonnes  down 21.5</p>
<p> 5  Germany		     16,679 tonnes  up   22.2</p>
<p> 6  United Arab Emirates    13,840 tonnes  up   25.5</p>
<p> 7  United Kingdom	    13,389 tonnes  down 20.3</p>
<p> 8  India			 12,757 tonnes  up    9.3</p>
<p> 9  Brazil			12,721 tonnes  down  6.5</p>
<p> 10 French West Indies	 9,881 tonnes  down  3.9</p>
<p> 11 Mexico			 9,878 tonnes  up   31.0</p>
<p> 12 Reunion			8,581 tonnes  down  1.4</p>
<p> 13 Saudi Arabia		 8,549 tonnes  up    3.3</p>
<p> 14 Italy			  7,807 tonnes  down  3.0</p>
<p> 15 Egypt			  7,403 tonnes  up    8.4</p>
<p> 16 Singapore		    6,822 tonnes  up    8.7</p>
<p> 17 South Africa		 6,566 tonnes  up    4.1</p>
<p> 18 Korea			  6,512 tonnes  down  2.8</p>
<p> 19 Thailand		     6,421 tonnes  down 10.5</p>
<p> 20 China			  6,002 tonnes  down 10.5</p>
<p> Total			   324,074 tonnes</p>
<p>Global January-October 1996 export traffic from the Paris airports totalled 484,155 tonnes in the first ten months of 1996, down 1.8 percent on the same period last year, airport authority figures show.</p>
<p>-- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
